  "note": "Re-judged 2026-11-03 by an independent auditor who authored none of 816ce1ce4c, 2cbd255ba4, 2e5c2d012a, d22b811ce4 or 1a2ccaeef8 (phase 5 of spec-filter-wire-0-umbrella, the per-peer text filter chain deleted). RFC 2545 Section 3 read: \"The link-local address shall be included in the Next Hop field if and only if the BGP speaker shares a common subnet with the entity identified by the global IPv6 address carried in the Network Address of Next Hop field and the peer the route is being advertised to.\" The one moved unit, TestRFC2545ForwardPolicyOwnGlobalJointSubnet, changed only its filter plumbing: The test filter is now an answerTransport behind filterTransportSeam, compiled by answerPolicy into a policychain library chain, so the verdict travels the real filter-update path (route.Input, rpc.FilterUpdateOutput decoded by the library chain) instead of the deleted policyFilterSeam that handed a PolicyResponse straight to the text chain; that is the production path every plugin filter now takes. The library chain calls the filter once per UPDATE, so the counter now counts every call and still requires exactly one, which still catches a writer that runs export policy twice. Every wire assertion is byte-identical: two sections on both rails (rs through rs-export), the native field exactly own global plus own link-local on the common link and own global alone off it, the legacy sibling NLRI and NEXT_HOP unchanged, production step order from buildOrderedEgressSteps. Producers linkLocalNextHop and thirdPartyLinkLocal are not changed by phase 5, so the declared scope stands. Verdict: partial. Tested: \"only if the BGP speaker shares a common subnet with the entity identified by the global IPv6 address carried in the Network Address of Next Hop field and the peer the route is being advertised to.\" Gap: \"The link-local address shall be included in the Next Hop field if\". Producer: internal/component/bgp/reactor/link_scope.go::thirdPartyLinkLocal, with linkLocalNextHop. Ran the tagged units under ./le job run at HEAD (-tags ze_bgp, -v): PASS (scratch audit-p5-units-v.log).",
